== 5.11 Chapter 5 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A reversible reaction is one in which],
  [the products can react to re-form the reactants],
  [a catalyst is always needed],
  [only one direction occurs],
  [the products cannot react back]
)

#mcq(2, [At dynamic equilibrium],
  [the products are used up],
  [the reaction has stopped],
  [the forward and reverse rates are equal and nonzero],
  [the reactants are used up]
)

#mcq(3, [Which statement about a system at equilibrium is NOT correct?],
  [the equilibrium can be disturbed],
  [the concentrations remain constant],
  [the reaction has stopped],
  [the rates of the forward and reverse reactions are equal]
)

#mcq(4, [For the reaction N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) ⇌ 2NH₃(g), increasing the pressure],
  [stops the reaction],
  [shifts the equilibrium to the left],
  [shifts the equilibrium to the right],
  [has no effect]
)

#mcq(5, [For the same Haber equilibrium, increasing the temperature],
  [has no effect],
  [doubles the yield],
  [shifts it to the right],
  [shifts it to the left]
)

#mcq(6, [The equilibrium constant K_c for N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃ is written as],
  [([N₂][H₂]³) ÷ [NH₃]²],
  [[NH₃]² ÷ ([N₂][H₂]³)],
  [[NH₃] ÷ ([N₂][H₂])],
  [[N₂][H₂] ÷ [NH₃]]
)

#mcq(7, [For H₂ + I₂ ⇌ 2HI, the equilibrium concentrations are [H₂] = 0.10, [I₂] = 0.10 and [HI] = 0.80 mol dm⁻³. K_c is],
  [80],
  [8.0],
  [64],
  [16]
)

#mcq(8, [The value of K_c for a reaction is 4.0 at 400 K and 40 at 500 K. The forward reaction is],
  [neither],
  [impossible],
  [endothermic],
  [exothermic]
)

#mcq(9, [Which change increases the equilibrium yield of products without changing K_c?],
  [adding a catalyst],
  [increasing the volume],
  [removing a product as it forms],
  [raising the temperature]
)

#mcq(10, [A catalyst added to a system at equilibrium],
  [increases the yield],
  [changes K_c],
  [decreases the yield],
  [has no effect on the position of equilibrium]
)

#mcq(11, [Le Chatelier's principle states that when a system at equilibrium is disturbed, the system],
  [changes its K_c],
  [shifts so as to oppose the change],
  [stops reacting],
  [always shifts to the right]
)

#mcq(12, [Increasing the volume of the vessel for N₂O₄(g) ⇌ 2NO₂(g) will],
  [favour N₂O₄],
  [stop the reaction],
  [have no effect],
  [favour NO₂]
)

#mcq(13, [Which of these equilibria is unaffected by a change in pressure?],
  [N₂O₄ ⇌ 2NO₂],
  [N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃],
  [H₂ + I₂ ⇌ 2HI],
  [2SO₂ + O₂ ⇌ 2SO₃]
)

#mcq(14, [For an exothermic reaction at equilibrium, raising the temperature],
  [increases K_c],
  [doubles K_c],
  [decreases K_c],
  [leaves K_c unchanged]
)

#mcq(15, [Which condition gives the highest equilibrium yield of ammonia in the Haber process?],
  [low pressure and low temperature],
  [high pressure and high temperature],
  [low pressure and high temperature],
  [high pressure and low temperature]
)

#mcq(16, [The temperature actually used in the Haber process is about 450 °C because],
  [ammonia decomposes],
  [the catalyst melts above 500 °C],
  [the yield is highest there],
  [the rate would be too slow at a lower temperature]
)

#mcq(17, [The catalyst used in the Haber process is],
  [iron],
  [vanadium(V) oxide],
  [platinum],
  [manganese(IV) oxide]
)

#mcq(18, [In the contact process, the catalyst is],
  [platinum],
  [nickel],
  [iron],
  [vanadium(V) oxide]
)

#mcq(19, [Which pressure is used in the contact process?],
  [about 1000 atm],
  [about 1–2 atm],
  [vacuum],
  [about 200 atm]
)

#mcq(20, [In an equilibrium mixture, if the concentration of a reactant is increased, the equilibrium shifts],
  [nowhere],
  [to the right],
  [to the products then back],
  [to the left]
)

#mcq(21, [When a chemical equilibrium is reached, the concentrations of reactants and products],
  [remain constant but are not necessarily equal],
  [become equal],
  [keep rising],
  [fall to zero]
)

#mcq(22, [For 2SO₂ + O₂ ⇌ 2SO₃, K_c has the units],
  [mol⁻¹ dm³],
  [mol² dm⁻⁶],
  [mol dm⁻³],
  [none]
)

#mcq(23, [An equilibrium mixture contains 0.20 mol dm⁻³ of A and 0.40 mol dm⁻³ of B for A ⇌ B. K_c is],
  [8.0],
  [2.0],
  [0.50],
  [0.20]
)

#mcq(24, [Which change would increase the amount of SO₃ in the contact process?],
  [raising the pressure],
  [raising the temperature],
  [lowering the pressure],
  [adding more catalyst]
)

#mcq(25, [Which statement about a saturated solution of a sparingly soluble salt in contact with the solid is correct?],
  [the dissolving has stopped],
  [the solution is unsaturated],
  [K_c does not apply],
  [it is a dynamic equilibrium]
)

#mcq(26, [If the value of K_c is very large, the equilibrium mixture contains],
  [mostly products],
  [equal amounts],
  [only reactants],
  [mostly reactants]
)

#mcq(27, [When the pressure on a gaseous equilibrium is reduced, the system shifts towards],
  [the side with fewer gas molecules],
  [the solid],
  [the liquid],
  [the side with more gas molecules]
)

#mcq(28, [Which factor does NOT appear in the expression for K_c?],
  [the concentration of a gas],
  [the concentration of a pure solid],
  [the concentration of a reactant],
  [the concentration of a product]
)

#mcq(29, [A reaction has K_c = 1.0 × 10⁻⁵ at 300 K. At equilibrium],
  [products predominate],
  [the reaction has stopped],
  [products and reactants are equal],
  [reactants predominate]
)

#mcq(30, [In the equilibrium 2NO₂(g) ⇌ N₂O₄(g) (brown to colourless), cooling a sealed tube makes it paler. The forward reaction is],
  [endothermic],
  [exothermic],
  [unaffected by temperature],
  [not reversible]
)

#mcq(31, [Which of these is an example of a dynamic equilibrium in a closed system?],
  [water in a sealed flask partly vapourised],
  [burning wood],
  [rusting of iron],
  [melting ice in an open dish]
)

#mcq(32, [Increasing the concentration of the product of a reversible reaction will],
  [shift it to the right],
  [shift the equilibrium to the left],
  [increase the yield],
  [increase K_c]
)

#mcq(33, [Which pair of conditions would give the lowest equilibrium yield of ammonia?],
  [450 °C, 200 atm],
  [500 °C, 300 atm],
  [600 °C, 50 atm],
  [300 °C, 200 atm]
)

#mcq(34, [For the equilibrium N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃, the effect of adding more nitrogen while keeping the pressure constant is to],
  [stop the reaction],
  [shift the equilibrium to the right],
  [change K_c],
  [shift it to the left]
)

#mcq(35, [What happens to the equilibrium position if a catalyst is removed from an exothermic equilibrium mixture?],
  [the reaction stops],
  [the yield falls],
  [the yield rises],
  [the yield is unchanged but equilibrium is reached more slowly]
)

#mcq(36, [The statement that a change in conditions is opposed by the system is known as],
  [Hess's law],
  [the law of mass action],
  [Boyle's law],
  [Le Chatelier's principle]
)

#mcq(37, [For H₂(g) + I₂(g) ⇌ 2HI(g), K_c = 64 at 700 K. If the equilibrium concentrations of H₂ and I₂ are both 0.20 mol dm⁻³, [HI] is],
  [3.2 mol dm⁻³],
  [6.4 mol dm⁻³],
  [1.6 mol dm⁻³],
  [2.5 mol dm⁻³]
)

#mcq(38, [A colourless gas dimerises exothermically. At constant temperature, increasing the pressure will],
  [favour the monomer],
  [have no effect],
  [favour the dimer],
  [give a different colour]
)

#mcq(39, [The equilibrium constant changes when],
  [more reactant is added],
  [the pressure changes],
  [the temperature changes],
  [a catalyst is added]
)

#mcq(40, [Which mixture reaches equilibrium fastest?],
  [one at low temperature with a catalyst],
  [one at low temperature with no catalyst],
  [one that is cooled],
  [one at high temperature with a catalyst]
)

